WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.795
<v Examiner>Define drug dependence.

2
00:00:02.795 --> 00:00:06.891
<v Examiner>What's the difference between psychological and physical dependence?

3
00:00:06.891 --> 00:00:07.855
<v Examiner>Give an example.

4
00:00:07.855 --> 00:00:08.578
<v Examiner>Three marks.

5
00:00:09.028 --> 00:00:10.507
This is the one she named.

6
00:00:10.507 --> 00:00:15.343
And it's the one with the error in her own answer key, so listen to this track twice.

7
00:00:15.793 --> 00:00:18.338
The hook: stop it, and the body protests.

8
00:00:18.338 --> 00:00:20.635
Withdrawal means physical dependence.

9
00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:22.629
Her slide's definition.

10
00:00:22.629 --> 00:00:28.335
Dependence is where a drug is pursued compulsively, without a therapeutic indication,

11
00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:34.376
that is, no medical need, and despite adverse effects: psychological, social, or physical.

12
00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:35.864
Then two kinds.

13
00:00:35.864 --> 00:00:40.641
Psychological dependence: out-of-control cravings, often with denial.

14
00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:45.279
Physical dependence: not using the drug causes withdrawal symptoms.

15
00:00:46.729 --> 00:00:47.965
Now her formative.

16
00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:49.955
Mini exam one, question four.

17
00:00:49.955 --> 00:00:55.651
Sione is reluctant to take his prescribed analgesic because he's scared of becoming

18
00:00:55.651 --> 00:00:56.338
dependent.

19
00:00:56.338 --> 00:00:59.426
Which description is accurate for dependence?

20
00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:05.191
Option B: experiencing withdrawal symptoms if a prescribed drug is stopped abruptly.

21
00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:09.858
Option C: a pattern of compulsive use with craving, loss of control,

22
00:01:09.858 --> 00:01:11.986
and continued use despite harm.

23
00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:13.358
Her document says C.

24
00:01:13.358 --> 00:01:18.162
In class, a student said C sounds more like addiction, and she agreed.

25
00:01:18.162 --> 00:01:22.898
Her words: addiction is compulsive use with craving, loss of control,

26
00:01:22.898 --> 00:01:24.820
continued use despite harms.

27
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.153
And she said the best answer is B,

28
00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:31.340
withdrawal symptoms if a prescribed drug is stopped abruptly.

29
00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.389
So in her exam: withdrawal when it's stopped is dependence.

30
00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:38.203
Compulsive use despite harm is addiction.

31
00:01:38.653 --> 00:01:39.407
The example.

32
00:01:39.407 --> 00:01:44.816
A person who has taken an opioid every day for months gets withdrawal symptoms if it's

33
00:01:44.816 --> 00:01:48.149
stopped suddenly, so it's weaned down slowly instead.

34
00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:51.356
And her point in class: there's medical dependence.

35
00:01:51.356 --> 00:01:53.305
You use your inhaler every day.

36
00:01:53.305 --> 00:01:54.626
Is that an addiction?

37
00:01:54.626 --> 00:01:54.815
No.

38
00:01:54.815 --> 00:01:57.707
Someone on insulin injections isn't an addict.

39
00:01:57.707 --> 00:02:00.349
They're dependent on a medicine they need.

40
00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:02.488
Where the marks go missing.

41
00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:05.428
One: picking the craving answer for dependence.

42
00:02:05.428 --> 00:02:06.492
That's addiction.

43
00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:09.620
Two: saying dependence means someone is an addict.

44
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:15.000
A person can be physically dependent on a prescribed medicine and not addicted at all.

45
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.503
That's exactly what Sione needs to hear.

46
00:02:17.953 --> 00:02:18.583
<v Examiner>Once more.

47
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:19.275
<v Examiner>Dependence.

48
00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:27.502
Dependence: a drug pursued compulsively, with no medical need, despite adverse effects.

49
00:02:27.502 --> 00:02:32.216
Psychological dependence is out-of-control cravings, often with denial.

50
00:02:32.216 --> 00:02:37.329
Physical dependence is withdrawal symptoms when the drug isn't used, her key:

51
00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:40.051
if a prescribed drug is stopped abruptly.

52
00:02:40.051 --> 00:02:45.495
An opioid taken for months and stopped suddenly causes withdrawal, so it's weaned.

53
00:02:45.495 --> 00:02:49.745
Insulin or a daily inhaler is medical dependence, not addiction.
